we're standing on level five  of park royal collection hickory but you  could also consider this a new ground  level  as you can see this level 5 accommodates  the pool deck  the spa the gym and a lot of communal  facilities for the hotel  the building actually incorporates more  greenery more than twice the amount of  greenery  than if you had left the site  undeveloped it's approximately fifteen  thousand square meters of green  surfaces which is roughly the equivalent  of  hong kong park right next to us so what  we wanted to investigate  is how a development in the city  can not only replace the greenery of the  city  but also intensify it by integrating the  sky gardens on every fourth floor we  break down the overall scale of the  building the greenery also helps to  frame the views for  the hotel room so the guests in their  hotel rooms enjoy kind of a  framed view and a lush green environment  almost like a resort feeling  even though we're smacking the city  center in a very dense urban environment  with a project we also aim to give back  to the city  so the building provides sheltered  walkways and cut-throughs  through the site for people to walk past  it also provides a beautiful backdrop  and a beautiful view for the housing  developments behind us  what's driving us in this integration of  landscape and architecture to answer  that you really have to look at the much  much bigger context of the  task and the challenges at hand it  really  is the fundamental question of how we  as a civilization want to live with  unsustainable urban development being  the major contributing factor to  co2 emissions and global energy  consumption  we really have a responsibility to  provide better solutions and to come up  with better typologies  how do we want to accommodate these  millions of people in our cities and how  can we reconcile that in our  relationship  with the natural environment and so  there are many many systems that are  affected by this it's  questions of how do we organize our  transport where and how do we harvest  energy and food how do we integrate  public space  we see our projects as prototypes for  the cities of the future  and singapore can play a really  important role  because not only are we forced to be  innovative because of the land scarcity  that we're facing but also because  of our geographic location climatic  condition  being located in the tropic means that  we can develop typologies here  for many of the new mega cities many of  them are located in the tropical belt  around the globe and yet most of the  existing typologies high density  typologies  are not developed for the tropical  climate zone  in this context integrating landscape  and greenery  in our development is absolutely key  [Music]
 

